# FROST SSH hardening drop-in — installed to /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-frost-hardening.conf
# (Arch's sshd_config `Include /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/*.conf` picks this up automatically.)
#
# frost-security.sh deploys this from the template below, but FLIPS
# PasswordAuthentication back to "yes" automatically if the target user
# has no ~/.ssh/authorized_keys — shipping "no" unconditionally would
# risk locking you out of a box with no other access method. Check the
# script's own log output to see which case applied.

PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
AuthenticationMethods publickey
MaxAuthTries 3
X11Forwarding no
AllowTcpForwarding no
ClientAliveInterval 300
ClientAliveCountMax 2
LoginGraceTime 20
